    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Assignment 4 — Data Pre-processing Pipeline\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Datasets:** Sonar.csv (208 instances, 60 features + class label) + HR_comma_sep.csv (14,999 records)  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Tools:** Google Colab, sklearn, pandas, matplotlib, seaborn  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Course:** Data Analytics — B.Tech ECE  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Overview\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This notebook implements a complete data pre-processing pipeline across four parts:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Part A:** Data Cleaning — Missing values, duplicates, IQR outlier detection, winsorization, type validation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Part B:** Data Integration & Transformation — Split/merge simulation, min-max normalization, z-score standardization, equal-width discretization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Part C:** Dimensionality Reduction on Sonar Data — PCA, explained variance, 2D scatter, t-SNE comparison\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Part D:** Feature Extraction & Reporting — Export PCA-reduced data for Power BI visualization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Key Finding:** PCA reduces 60 sonar features to ~46 components explaining 90% variance; t-SNE provides superior class separation compared to PCA in 2D embedding space.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Setup — Install & Load\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Install required packages\\n\",\n",
    "    \"!pip install -q gdown\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Download HR dataset from Google Drive\\n\",\n",
    "    \"!gdown \\\"https://drive.google.com/uc?id=1bviXba_EF5Sqv_RzUUtquON5KUrdrjjj\\\" -O \\\"HR_comma_sep.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Import libraries\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import seaborn as sns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, MinMaxScaler\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from sklearn.manifold import TSNE\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import warnings\\n\",\n",
    "    \"warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from IPython.display import display, Markdown\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set style\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.set_style(\\\"whitegrid\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (10, 6)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.rcParams['font.size'] = 12\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"✅ Setup complete!\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part A — Data Cleaning [4 Marks]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Load HR Dataset\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"df_hr = pd.read_csv(\\\"HR_comma_sep.csv\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_hr.columns = ['satisfaction_level', 'last_evaluation', 'number_project',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                  'average_montly_hours', 'time_spend_company', 'Work_accident',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                  'left', 'promotion_last_5years', 'Department', 'salary']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"**Shape:** {df_hr.shape}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_hr.head()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 27: Check Missing Values, Duplicates, and Outliers\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"### Task 27 — Missing Values, Duplicates & Outlier Report\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# 1. Missing values\\n\",\n",
    "    \"missing = df_hr.isnull().sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"missing_total = missing.sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"**Missing Values:** {missing_total}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"```\\\\n{missing.to_string()}\\\\n```\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# 2. Duplicate rows\\n\",\n",
    "    \"duplicates = df_hr.duplicated().sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"**Duplicate Rows:** {duplicates}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# 3. IQR-based outlier detection on numeric columns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"numeric_cols = ['satisfaction_level', 'last_evaluation', 'number_project',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                'average_montly_hours', 'time_spend_company']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"outlier_report = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"total_outliers = 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for col in numeric_cols:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Q1 = df_hr[col].quantile(0.25)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Q3 = df_hr[col].quantile(0.75)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    IQR = Q3 - Q1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    lower_bound = Q1 - 1.5 * IQR\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    upper_bound = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    outlier_count = len(df_hr[(df_hr[col] < lower_bound) | (df_hr[col] > upper_bound)])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    total_outliers += outlier_count\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    outlier_report.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Column': col,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Q1': round(Q1, 3),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Q3': round(Q3, 3),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'IQR': round(IQR, 3),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Lower Bound': round(lower_bound, 3),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Upper Bound': round(upper_bound, 3),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Outlier Count': outlier_count\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"outlier_df = pd.DataFrame(outlier_report)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(outlier_df.style.set_table_attributes('style=\\\"font-size: 11px\\\"'))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"**Total Outliers (IQR method):** {total_outliers}\\\"))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 28: Remove Duplicates & Winsorize Outliers\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"### Task 28 — Duplicate Removal & Winsorization\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Remove duplicates\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_hr_clean = df_hr.drop_duplicates().copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"removed = len(df_hr) - len(df_hr_clean)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"**Duplicates removed:** {removed}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"**Shape before:** {df_hr.shape} → **Shape after:** {df_hr_clean.shape}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Winsorization on average_montly_hours at 5th and 95th percentile\\n\",\n",
    "    \"lower_cap = df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours'].quantile(0.05)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"upper_cap = df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours'].quantile(0.95)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"**Winsorization bounds:** Lower = {lower_cap:.1f}, Upper = {upper_cap:.1f}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours_winsorized'] = df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours'].clip(lower=lower_cap, upper=upper_cap)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Compare histograms before and after\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 5))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].hist(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours'], bins=50, edgecolor='black', color='salmon', alpha=0.8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].axvline(lower_cap, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, label=f'5th %ile ({lower_cap:.0f})')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].axvline(upper_cap, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, label=f'95th %ile ({upper_cap:.0f})')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].set_title('Before Winsorization', fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].set_xlabel('Average Monthly Hours')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].set_ylabel('Frequency')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].hist(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours_winsorized'], bins=50, edgecolor='black', color='teal', alpha=0.8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].axvline(lower_cap, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, label=f'5th %ile ({lower_cap:.0f})')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].axvline(upper_cap, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, label=f'95th %ile ({upper_cap:.0f})')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].set_title('After Winsorization (5th-95th %ile)', fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].set_xlabel('Average Monthly Hours')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].set_ylabel('Frequency')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.suptitle('Histogram Comparison: Before vs After Winsorization', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.savefig('partA_winsorization_before_after.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Statistics comparison\\n\",\n",
    "    \"stats_comparison = pd.DataFrame({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'Statistic': ['Mean', 'Std Dev', 'Min', 'Max', 'Skewness'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'Before': [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours'].mean(), 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours'].std(), 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours'].min(), 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours'].max(), 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours'].skew(), 4)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'After': [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours_winsorized'].mean(), 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours_winsorized'].std(), 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours_winsorized'].min(), 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours_winsorized'].max(), 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        round(df_hr_clean['average_montly_hours_winsorized'].skew(), 4)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(stats_comparison)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"**Observation:** Winsorization reduces extreme values at both tails, bringing skewness closer to zero and reducing standard deviation. The distribution becomes more symmetric.\\\"))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 29: Check Data Type Consistency\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"### Task 29 — Data Type Consistency Check\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Check for issues\\n\",\n",
    "    \"type_issues = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Check binary columns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"binary_cols = ['Work_accident', 'left', 'promotion_last_5years']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for col in binary_cols:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if df_hr_clean[col].dtype != 'int64' and df_hr_clean[col].dtype != 'int32':\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        type_issues.append(f\\\"  - '{col}' converted to 'int64'\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        df_hr_clean[col] = df_hr_clean[col].astype(int)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Check categorical columns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if df_hr_clean['Department'].dtype != 'category':\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df_hr_clean['Department'] = df_hr_clean['Department'].astype('category')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    type_issues.append(f\\\"  - 'Department' converted to 'category'\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if df_hr_clean['salary'].dtype != 'category':\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df_hr_clean['salary'] = df_hr_clean['salary'].astype('category')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    type_issues.append(f\\\"  - 'salary' converted to 'category'\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if type_issues:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    display(Markdown(\\\"**Changes Made:**\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for issue in type_issues:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        display(Markdown(issue))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    display(Markdown(\\\"**No data type issues found.**\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"**Final Data Types:**\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(df_hr_clean.dtypes.to_frame(name='Dtype'))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part B — Data Integration & Transformation [4 Marks]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 30: Simulate Data Integration (Split & Re-merge)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"### Task 30 — Data Integration Simulation\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cols_first5 = ['satisfaction_level', 'last_evaluation', 'number_project', 'average_montly_hours', 'time_spend_company']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cols_last5 = ['Work_accident', 'left', 'promotion_last_5years', 'Department', 'salary']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Split into two halves\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_half1 = df_hr_clean[cols_first5].copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_half2 = df_hr_clean[cols_last5].copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Add index for merging\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_half1['_merge_idx'] = df_half1.index\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_half2['_merge_idx'] = df_half2.index\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"**Half 1 shape:** {df_half1.shape} | **Half 2 shape:** {df_half2.shape}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Re-merge on common index\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_merged = pd.merge(df_half1, df_half2, on='_merge_idx', how='inner')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_merged = df_merged.drop('_merge_idx', axis=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"**Merged shape:** {df_merged.shape}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f\\\"✅ **Verification:** Rows match = {df_merged.shape[0] == df_hr_clean.shape[0]}\\\"))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 31: Min-Max Normalization\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"### Task 31 — Min-Max Normalization\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"norm_cols = ['satisfaction_level', 'last_evaluation', 'average_montly_hours']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Before stats\\n\",\n",
    "    \"before_stats = df_hr_clean[norm_cols].describe().T[['mean', 'std', 'min', 'max']].round(4)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"before_stats.columns = ['Before_Mean', 'Before_Std', 'Before_Min', 'Before_Max']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Apply min-max normalization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"minmax_scaler = MinMaxScaler()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_hr_clean[[c + '_minmax' for c in norm_cols]] = minmax_scaler.fit_transform(df_hr_clean[norm_cols])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# After stats\\n\",\n",
    "    \"after_stats = df_hr_clean[[c + '_minmax' for c in norm_cols]].describe().T[['mean', 'std', 'min', 'max']].round(4)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"after_stats.columns = ['After_Mean', 'After_Std', 'After_Min', 'After_Max']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"combined_stats = pd.concat([before_stats, after_stats], axis=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(combined_stats)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"**Observation:** All values scaled to [0, 1] range. Relative distances preserved proportionally.\\\"))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 32: Z-Score Standardization & Box Plots\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"### Task 32 — Z-Score Standardization\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Apply z-score standardization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"zscore_scaler = StandardScaler()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_hr_clean[[c + '_zscore' for c in norm_cols]] = zscore_scaler.fit_transform(df_hr_clean[norm_cols])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# After z-score stats\\n\",\n",
    "    \"zscore_stats = df_hr_clean[[c + '_zscore' for c in norm_cols]].describe().T[['mean', 'std', 'min', 'max']].round(4)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"zscore_stats.columns = ['ZScore_Mean', 'ZScore_Std', 'ZScore_Min', 'ZScore_Max']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"combined_stats2 = pd.concat([before_stats, zscore_stats], axis=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(combined_stats2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\\"**Observation:** Mean ≈ 0, Std ≈ 1. Values represent standard deviations from mean.\\\"))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Side-by-side box plots\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Original\\n\",\n",
    "    \"bp1 = df_hr_clean[norm_cols].boxplot(ax=axes[0], patch_artist=True, return_type='dict')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for bp, color in zip(bp1['boxes'], ['#3498db', '#2ecc71', '#e74c3c']):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    bp.set_facecolor(color)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].set_title('Original Data', fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].tick_params(axis='x', rotation=30)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Min-Max\\n\",\n",
    "    \"bp2 = df_hr_clean[[c + '_minmax' for c in norm_cols]].boxplot(ax=axes[1], patch_artist=True, return_type='dict')\\n\",\n",
